In article <6877@cg-atla.UUCP> granger@cg-atla.UUCP (Pete Granger) writes:
>Suggestion for future versions: If a ghost kills you, it shouldn't still be
>around in the bones file. Ghosts should be freed from this plane once they've
>avenged themselves in some way. Future players would find the loot from the
>first ghost (still cursed), plus the second ghost and all its loot. Of course,
>if you were killed by something else, you'd still have multiple ghosts on
>the level.
>-- 
>Pete Granger    ...!{ulowell,ginosko,decvax,ism780c,ima}!cg-atla!granger

No, no, no!  One of the best things in the game is the possibility that a
truely killer level from hell can be created as players arrive on a bones
level and die from the ghosts of their predecessors.  Of course, the loot also
gets impressive and the payoff from these levels balances their danger,
somewhat.  If what you suggest is implemented, then the loot would continue to
pile up while there is onle one ghost (assuming the ghost kills you off).  I
think there have been enough modifications to make NetHack *easier*.  (Coming
from a purist who doesn't like playing games with Stooges, Kops, #sacrifice,
etc. I'm surprised that you feel this way! :-)

